# Normalise line endings.
#
# Every text blob in this repository is stored with LF. Without this file a
# contributor with `core.autocrlf=true` (Git for Windows' default) gets CRLF in
# the working tree. Git hides the drift, because it normalises on read, so
# `git status` stays clean -- but tools that read raw bytes do not. Prettier,
# via `npm run validate:articles`, reports every affected article as
# "not formatted" for reasons unrelated to its content.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF regardless of a contributor's local
# autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets. `text=auto` detects these on its own; listing them makes the
# intent explicit and stops Git from ever sniffing them as text.
*.avif binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.jpg  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
